        // owned table — on Laravel 11+ it is created by the default
        // `create_users_table` migration, and `up()` above only fills the gap
        // when it is absent. Dropping it on rollback would destroy the host's
        // live session storage (and `migrate` would not recreate it, since the
        // framework migration is already run). Remove the table by hand if you
        // truly need to.
    }

    /**
     * Resolve the user-id column shape of the users who sign in.
     *
     * Returns one of `bigint`, `uuid`, `ulid`, `string`. Inlined in each
     * Martis migration stub so the published file works even if the package
     * itself is later removed from the host's composer.
     */
    private function resolveUserKey(): string
    {
